they might have discovered it at night.\n\nC) No other butterfly species lives in this region of central america.\n- This assumption is not necessary to explain why the scientists discovered the butterfly at night. The fact that the butterfly is green and matches the foliage during the day is enough to explain why they might have discovered it at night.\n\nD) The foliage in the butterfly's habitat is completely green.\n- This assumption is necessary to explain why the scientists discovered the butterfly at night. If the foliage in the butterfly's habitat is not completely green, the butterfly's green color would not match the foliage, and it would be more likely to be discovered during the day. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
