messages:    8%|7         | 46/600 [00:22<03:35,  2.57it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA certain meeting invited six people from a certain workplace: Zhang, Wang, Li, Zhao, Sun, and Zhou to attend. However, due to work arrangements, all six people cannot go to the meeting at the same time. Among them: Only one person between Zhang and Zhao can attend the meeting; Also Only one person between Li and Zhao can attend the meeting; At least one person between Zhang and Wang can attend the meeting; Two of the three among Zhang, Sun, and Zhou can attend the meeting; Wang and Li either both attend the meeting or neither of them attend the meeting; if Zhao will not attend the meeting, then Sun will not attend the meeting either.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to this arrangement, Which one probably will not attend the meeting in the end?\n# Options:\nA) Zhang and wang\nB) Wang and li\nC) Li and zhao\nD) Zhao and sun', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, we need to analyze the given conditions and determine which pair of individuals is most likely to not attend the meeting. Let's break down the information step by step:.\n\n1. **Only one person between Zhang and Zhao can attend the meeting.**.\n   - This means either Zhang or Zhao will attend, but not both.\n\n2. **Only one person between Li and Zhao can attend the meeting.**.\n   - This means either Li or Zhao will attend, but not both.\n\n3. **At least one person between Zhang and Wang can attend the meeting.**.\n   - This means either Zhang or Wang will attend, but not both.\n\n4. **Two of the three among Zhang, Sun, and Zhou can attend the meeting.**.\n   - This means either Zhang and Sun, Zhang and Zhou, or Sun and Zhou can attend, but not all three.\n\n5. **Wang and Li either both attend the meeting or neither of them attend the meeting.**.\n   - This means if Wang attends, Li must also attend, and vice versa.\n\n6. **If Zhao will not attend the meeting, then Sun will not attend the meeting either.**.\n   - This means if Zhao does not attend, Sun must also not attend.\n\nNow, let's consider the possible scenarios based on these conditions:.\n\n- If Zhao attends, then Sun must also attend (from condition 6).\n- If Zhao does not attend, then Sun must also not attend (from condition 6).\n- If Zhang and Zhao both attend, then Li and Wang cannot both attend (from condition 1).\n- If Zhang and Wang both attend, then Li and Zhao cannot both attend (from condition 3).\n- If Zhang and Sun both attend, then Li and Zhao cannot both attend (from condition 4).\n- If Zhang and Zhou both attend, then Li and Zhao cannot both attend (from condition 4).\n- If Sun and Zhou both attend, then Li and Zhao cannot both attend (from condition 4).\n\nGiven these constraints, let's evaluate the options:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
