messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAutism affects social interaction, language communication, hobbies and other aspects of behavior. Researchers have discovered that if the neuronectin protein in the experimental mice is synthesized too much, it can lead to autism. Therefore, they believe that autism has an important relationship with the amount of neuroconnect protein synthesis.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, best supports the above view?\n# Options:\nA) Laboratory rats living in groups are less likely to suffer from autism than those living alone\nB) The proportion of male laboratory rats suffering from autism is 5 times that of female laboratory rats\nC) Inhibition of neuronectin protein synthesis can relieve autism symptoms in experimental mice\nD) If the key genes that control protein synthesis in experimental mice are removed, the neuronectin in their bodies will increase', "<think>.\nTo determine which option best supports the view that autism has an important relationship with the amount of neuroconnect protein synthesis, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Laboratory rats living in groups are less likely to suffer from autism than those living alone - This option suggests that social interaction may play a role in autism, but it does not directly address the relationship between neuroconnect protein synthesis and autism.\n\nB) The proportion of male laboratory rats suffering from autism is 5 times that of female laboratory rats - This option provides information about the prevalence of autism in males and females, but it does not directly address the relationship between neuroconnect protein synthesis and autism.\n\nC) Inhibition of neuronectin protein synthesis can relieve autism symptoms in experimental mice - This option directly supports the view that autism has an important relationship with the amount of neuroconnect protein synthesis, as it suggests that reducing the synthesis of this protein can alleviate autism symptoms.\n\nD) If the key genes that control protein synthesis in experimental mice are removed, the neuronectin in their bodies will increase - This option suggests that removing key genes controlling protein synthesis can lead to an increase in neuronectin, but it does not directly address the relationship between neuroconnect protein synthesis and autism. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
