messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n3D stereoscopic technology represents the cutting-edge level of the current film technology, because the film to achieve a highly credible sense of space, it may become the mainstream of future films. Although the screen characters in 3D movies are computer-generated, the performances of computer characters that include actions and expressions are based on the performances of real actors, just like makeup technology in the digital age. This has also aroused the concern of some actors: with the development of computer technology, computer-generated images and animations will replace live-action performances in the future.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, can most reduce the actor's worries?\n# Options:\nA) All film directors can only communicate with real people, not with computers\nB) The shooting of any film depends on the choice of the producer, and the actors can keep up with the development of the times\nC) The current high box office of 3d movies is only the result of people's temporary novelty, and the future is still unknown\nD) The film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, and its form of expression has nothing to do with the preferences of the director", "<think>.\nTo answer this question, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) All film directors can only communicate with real people, not with computers.\n- This statement suggests that film directors cannot communicate with computers, which implies that they would not be able to use 3D technology effectively. However, this is not necessarily true, as many film directors have already used 3D technology in their films. Therefore, this option does not reduce the actor's worries.\n\nB) The shooting of any film depends on the choice of the producer, and the actors can keep up with the development of the times.\n- This statement implies that the producer's choice of technology does not affect the actors' ability to keep up with the times. While this may be true, it does not directly address the actor's concerns about the future of 3D technology. Therefore, this option does not reduce the actor's worries.\n\nC) The current high box office of 3d movies is only the result of people's temporary novelty, and the future is still unknown.\n- This statement suggests that the popularity of 3D movies is not sustainable in the long term. While this may be true, it does not directly address the actor's concerns about the future of 3D technology. Therefore, this option does not reduce the actor's worries.\n\nD) The film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, and its form of expression has nothing to do with the preferences of the director. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
