ts into cement in high-temperature kilns uses large amounts of energy. Since oil is a common source of energy, it is reasonable to infer that oil is used as a source of energy for some of the kilns. This statement can be logically inferred from the context.\n   - **C) The higher the price of cement rises, the higher the price of clay rises.**.\n     - The context does not provide any information about how changes in cement prices affect the price of clay. Therefore, we cannot logically infer this statement from the given information.\n   - **D) Oil is one of the basic ingredients that make up cement.**.\n     - The context states that the basic ingredients for cement include limestone and clay. While oil is mentioned as a source of energy, it is not explicitly stated that oil is one of the basic ingredients that make up cement. Therefore, we cannot logically infer this statement from the given information.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
