 diagnosis of the disease based on the patient's oral materials - This option describes a quick and intuitive approach to making a diagnosis. The doctor uses the patient's oral materials to make a diagnosis without necessarily following a structured process. This is typical intuitive thinking, as it involves making a quick and direct judgment based on available information. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
