messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe term boundary problem refers to various short-sighted behaviors of employees due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises, and the harm caused by such behaviors to the enterprise\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings belongs to the term boundary problem\n# Options:\nA) Because he will retire in one year, lao zhao feels unable and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse\nB) Because he was not familiar with the business, xiao li, who had just come a month, lost a big customer and the company lost a lot\nC) Because he felt that it was impossible to become a regular worker,xiao wang worked hard every day to show himself \nD) Because he only signed a contract for half a year, xiao sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipment', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, let's analyze each option and see if it fits the definition of the term boundary problem.\n\nA) Lao Zhao feels unable due to his short-term employment. This could be a boundary problem because he might be experiencing stress or anxiety about his future with the company, which could affect his work efficiency.\n\nB) Xiao Li lost a big customer due to his lack of familiarity with the business. This could be a boundary problem because he might not have had enough time to learn the business well enough to make informed decisions, leading to mistakes.\n\nC) Xiao Wang worked hard every day to show himself. This doesn't seem to fit the definition of a boundary problem, as it seems like a positive effort rather than a short-sighted behavior.\n\nD) Xiao Sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipment. This could be a boundary problem because he might not have understood the importance of using the equipment properly, leading to potential safety hazards or damage to the equipment. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
