messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn our solar system only one of the nine planets -- Earth -- qualifies as fit to sustain life. Nonetheless, using this ratio, and considering the astonishingly large number of planetary systems in the universe, we must conclude that the number of planets fit to sustain some form of life is extremely large.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the argument is questionable because it presumes which one of the following without providing justification?\n# Options:\nA) Life similar to earth's could evolve under conditions very different from those on earth.\nB) If a planet is earthlike, then life will arise on it.\nC) Our solar system is similar to many other planetary systems in the universe.\nD) Most other planetary systems in the universe have nine planets.", "<think>.\nTo determine which option the argument presumes without providing justification, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Life similar to Earth's could evolve under conditions very different from those on Earth.\n- This option suggests that life could evolve under different conditions, which is a reasonable assumption. However, the argument does not provide any evidence or justification for this assumption.\n\nB) If a planet is Earthlike, then life will arise on it.\n- This option implies a deterministic relationship between Earth-like conditions and the presence of life. The argument does not provide any evidence or justification for this assumption.\n\nC) Our solar system is similar to many other planetary systems in the universe.\n- This option suggests that our solar system is representative of other planetary systems in the universe. The argument does not provide any evidence or justification for this assumption.\n\nD) Most other planetary systems in the universe have nine planets. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
