s assigned to the sales department, it does not violate any conditions. Therefore, this statement can be true.\n   - **Option B: H is assigned to the production department.**.\n     - If H is assigned to the production department, it does not violate any conditions. Therefore, this statement can be true.\n   - **Option C: I was assigned to the sales department.**.\n     - If I is assigned to the sales department, it does not violate any conditions. Therefore, this statement can be true.\n   - **Option D: W was assigned to the public relations department.**.\n     - If W is assigned to the public relations department, it does not violate any conditions. However, we need to check if this is possible given the constraints. Since X and F are in the production department, W cannot be in the production department (from condition 3). Therefore, W must be in the sales department. This means W cannot be in the public relations department. Thus, this statement cannot be true.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
