oncept of field independence, as individuals driven by intrinsic motivation tend to process information independently of external influences.\n\n4. **Option D: Doing things is dominated by external motivation**.\n   - External motivation involves doing something because of external rewards or pressures. This aligns with the concept of field dependence, as individuals influenced by external motivation are more likely to process information based on external references. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
