messages:   75%|#######4  | 449/600 [14:47<01:33,  1.62it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAvoidance conditioning refers to when a situation of disgust or unhappiness arises, the individual reacts in a way that escapes the situation of disgust or unhappiness. Then the probability of this reaction occurring in similar scenarios later increases.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is not avoidance conditioning?\n# Options:\nA) Detour after seeing the garbage on the road\nB) When you hit something hot, quickly withdraw your hand\nC) Leave temporarily when you feel noisy in the house\nD) Afraid to meet strangers and dare not go to the streets', "<think>.\nTo determine which option is not avoidance conditioning, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Detour after seeing the garbage on the road: This option involves avoiding a situation (seeing garbage on the road) by taking a detour. This is an example of avoidance conditioning because the individual is reacting to a situation of disgust (seeing garbage) by taking a different route to avoid it.\n\nB) When you hit something hot, quickly withdraw your hand: This option involves avoiding a situation (hitting something hot) by withdrawing your hand quickly. This is also an example of avoidance conditioning because the individual is reacting to a situation of discomfort (hitting something hot) by withdrawing their hand to avoid further discomfort.\n\nC) Leave temporarily when you feel noisy in the house: This option involves avoiding a situation (feeling noisy in the house) by leaving temporarily. This is an example of avoidance conditioning because the individual is reacting to a situation of discomfort (feeling noisy) by leaving the house to avoid it.\n\nD) Afraid to meet strangers and dare not go to the streets: This option involves avoiding a situation (meeting strangers) by not going to the streets. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
