s Jiangnan, and no other team can be the champion. If Jiangnan is the champion, then Statements (1), (2), and (4) would all be incorrect, leaving only Statement (3) as the correct statement. This satisfies the condition that only one statement is correct.\n  \n- If Statement (4) is correct, then the champion is not Shannan. This means the champion could be either Jiangnan, Shanbei, or Jiangbei. However, if the champion is Jiangnan, then Statement (3) would be correct, which contradicts the condition that only one statement is correct. Therefore, Statement (4) cannot be the correct statement.\n\nBased on this analysis, the only statement that can be correct without contradicting the condition is Statement (3). Therefore, the champion is Jiangnan.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
