med to regular exercise do not gain weight when they stop exercising.\n- This option implies that regular exercise can prevent weight gain in nonsmokers, which is relevant to the context because it suggests that exercise might be a healthy alternative to smoking, potentially reducing the stress associated with quitting smoking and preventing weight gain.\n\nD) Aerobic exercise can stimulate the brain's production of endorphins, which reduce tension.\n- This option suggests that aerobic exercise can reduce tension, which is relevant to the context because it implies that exercise might be a healthy alternative to smoking, potentially reducing the stress associated with quitting smoking.\n\nBased on the analysis, option B) Each group in the study included four hundred randomly selected participants. does not provide support for the argument because it does not directly address the relationship between exercise and quitting smoking. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
