messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nPublic opinion: it refers to the opinions expressed by a considerable number of individuals, groups or organizations on public affairs\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings belongs to public opinion:\n# Options:\nA) All the leading members of a company attended the meeting to introduce the development prospect of the company to the new employees\nB) After the collective return of pilots in an airline, many passengers thought that these pilots were not responsible for the safety of passengers and expressed their unwillingness to take the airline's plane\nC) Li yong's relatives and friends unanimously praised the new house purchased by his family\nD) Gao shan expressed different opinions on a decision of the company", '<think>.\nTo determine which option belongs to public opinion, we need to consider the definition provided: "Public opinion refers to the opinions expressed by a considerable number of individuals, groups, or organizations on public affairs." Let\'s analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) All the leading members of a company attended the meeting to introduce the development prospect of the company to the new employees.\n- This option involves a group of individuals (the leading members of the company) expressing their opinions on a specific topic (the development prospect of the company). However, it does not involve a considerable number of individuals, groups, or organizations expressing their opinions on public affairs. Therefore, this option does not fit the definition of public opinion.\n\nB) After the collective return of pilots in an airline, many passengers thought that these pilots were not responsible for the safety of passengers and expressed their unwillingness to take the airline\'s plane.\n- This option involves a considerable number of individuals (passengers) expressing their opinions on a specific topic (the safety of the airline\'s pilots). The opinions are related to public affairs (the safety of passengers) and are expressed by a considerable number of individuals. Therefore, this option fits the definition of public opinion.\n\nC) Li yong\'s relatives and friends unanimously praised the new house purchased by his family.\n- This option involves a group of individuals (Li yong\'s relatives and friends) expressing their opinions on a specific topic (the new house purchased by his family). However, it does not involve a considerable number of individuals, groups, or organizations expressing their opinions on public affairs. Therefore, this option does not fit the definition of public opinion.\n\nD) Gao shan expressed different opinions on a decision of the company.\n- This option involves an individual (Gao shan) expressing their opinions on a specific topic (a decision of the company). However, it does not involve a considerable number of individuals, groups, or organizations expressing their opinions on public affairs. Therefore, this option does not fit the definition of public opinion. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
