 describes a situation where a manager is being criticized for maintaining an unprofessional environment. While this could be seen as a negative impression, it does not involve the manager actively trying to manage their own impression but rather being negatively evaluated by others.\n\n3. **Option C**: "After hearing his classmates secretly say bad things about him, Lin couldn\'t help but go up and beat him." This option describes a physical altercation between individuals, which is not related to impression management. It is more about conflict resolution rather than managing one\'s public image.\n\n4. **Option D**: "Before the interview, in order to be hired, Xiao Li in the clothing, hairstyle, and so on has made careful preparation." This option describes a candidate preparing for an interview by dressing appropriately. While this might be seen as a form of impression management, it is more about ensuring a positive first impression rather than actively managing one\'s public image. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
