 - This statement aligns with Edward's view that governments can redistribute resources via taxation if they permit emigration. Raphaela would disagree with this because she believes forcing people to help others is morally wrong.\n\nC) **Any government that redistributes resources via taxation forces people to help others.**.\n   - This statement aligns with Raphaela's view that forcing people to help others is morally wrong. Edward would disagree with this because he believes governments can redistribute resources via taxation if they permit emigration.\n\nD) **Every government should allow people to help others voluntarily.**.\n   - This statement aligns with both Raphaela's and Edward's views. Both believe that people should be allowed to help others voluntarily without coercion.\n\nBased on the analysis, Raphaela and Edward disagree on the truth of option B: **Any government that permits emigration has the right to redistribute resources via taxation.** Raphaela would disagree with this statement because she believes forcing people to help others is morally wrong, while Edward supports it. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
